    "body": "LOGICAL_AGENT = LYNCH\nASSIGNED_BY = JINGO\nSTATUS = ACTIVE RESEARCH\nROLE_STATUS = PROPOSED / TRIAL REQUIRED\n\n## OWNER INTENT\nSPARX requires LYNCH to learn how to build locations correctly for ZB — not merely place a camera inside an already-finished room.\n\n## AUTHORIZED RESEARCH SCOPE\nStudy current professional/public material and production practice on:\n- production design and set design for film/animation;\n- location architecture for dramatic staging;\n- spatial dramaturgy: how space creates pressure, hierarchy, concealment, reveal, pursuit, confrontation and release;\n- floor plans, circulation, entrances/exits, choke points, sightlines, eyelines and action axes;\n- foreground / midground / background construction and depth planning;\n- scale, proportions and human readability of spaces;\n- verticality: stairs, balconies, drops, levels, overlooks and layered movement;\n- how architecture supports blocking, camera, lenses, shot sizes and editing continuity;\n- practical/motivated lighting-source placement as part of location design;\n- modular/reusable set construction and production-efficient environment design;\n- animation layout / background / multiplane / limited-animation location planning;\n- previs, storyboard, 3D blockout and virtual production approaches;\n- game/real-time environment techniques useful for cinematic locations where relevant;\n- mature open-source tools, libraries, Blender add-ons, asset/layout systems and integration methods that can increase ZB speed and quality.\n\n## CORE LAW\n`LOCATION IS A DRAMATIC MACHINE — NOT A DECORATIVE BACKDROP.`\n\nFor every studied location method ask:\n`WHAT CAN CHARACTERS DO HERE?`\n`WHAT CAN THE CAMERA SEE HERE?`\n`WHAT CAN BE HIDDEN / REVEALED HERE?`\n`HOW DOES MOVEMENT CHANGE POWER?`\n`HOW DOES LIGHT EXPLAIN OR DISTORT THE SPACE?`\n`CAN THIS LOCATION PRODUCE MULTIPLE STRONG SCENES WITHOUT REDESIGN?`\n\n## REQUIRED OUTPUT\nPost findings here as durable research passes:\n\n`LYNCH_LOCATION_RESEARCH_PASS`\n`TOPIC = ...`\n`SPATIAL PRINCIPLE = ...`\n`DRAMATIC USE = ...`\n`CAMERA / BLOCKING USE = ...`\n`LIGHTING USE = ...`\n`PRODUCTION USE = ...`\n`SOURCE BASIS = ...`\n`REUSE TOOL / METHOD = ... | NONE`\n`ACTION = ADOPT_METHOD | EVALUATE_TOOL | REJECT | NEEDS_JINGO_REVIEW`\n\nAfter enough research, produce one compact:\n`ZB LOCATION CONSTRUCTION METHOD R01 — PROPOSAL`\ncovering the sequence:\n`SCENE NEED → DRAMATIC SPACE → FLOOR PLAN → MOVEMENT PATHS → SIGHTLINES → LEVELS/DEPTH → LIGHT SOURCES → CAMERA ACCESS → MODULAR BUILD → CONTINUITY/QC`.\n\n## HARD BOUNDARIES\nResearch and propose methods freely, but do NOT silently change an approved ZB location or invent canonical architecture for an active scene. Canonical location changes remain proposal-only until approved by the proper gate.\n\n`LYNCH MAY DESIGN A LOCATION PROPOSAL.`\n`LYNCH MAY NOT SELF-APPROVE LOCATION CANON.`\n\nREUSE-FIRST remains mandatory: search mature existing tools/methods before proposing custom technical systems.",
